🚽 Test case: #197 -- a two-level pointer-field chain (`a.next.next.val`)
🚽 proves the fix is genuinely recursive, not special-cased for a single
🚽 hop. Each `.next` follows a `gang Node *` field; the final `.val`
🚽 read/write lands in the third node's storage (c.val reflects the
🚽 write-through).
gang Node {
    rizz val;
    gang Node *next;
};

skibidi main {
    gang Node a;
    gang Node b;
    gang Node c;
    a.val = 1;
    b.val = 2;
    c.val = 3;
    a.next = &b;
    b.next = &c;
    yapping("%d", a.next.next.val);
    a.next.next.val = 42;
    yapping("%d", c.val);
}
